  "sections": [
    {
      "section_id": "pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_section_1",
      "section_title": "Pediatric emergency dosing tape/chart",
      "section_order": 1,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "subsection_id": "pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_subsection_1",
          "subsection_title": "Overview",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_group_1",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/instrumentation/pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_01.webp",
                  "caption": null
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_subsection_2",
          "subsection_title": "1. Identification",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_group_2",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "A pediatric emergency dosing tape or chart is a clinical aid used to estimate a child’s weight from body length and guide emergency medication dosing and equipment selection when an accurate weight is not readily available."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "A well-known example is the Broselow Pediatric Emergency Tape."
                },
                {
                  "type": "list",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "Classification: Pediatric emergency assessment and resuscitation aid.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Principle: Length-based estimation of weight, often linked to color-coded dosing and equipment recommendations.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Key identifying feature: A measuring tape with length markings and, on many models, color-coded zones corresponding to estimated weight ranges.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Typical setting: Emergency departments, resuscitation rooms, ambulances and pediatric emergency trolleys.",
                      "level": 0
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Examiner’s key point: It estimates weight; it does not measure actual body weight."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_subsection_3",
          "subsection_title": "2. Uses and indications",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_group_3",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "list",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "Estimating weight during pediatric emergencies when weighing the child is impractical or would delay treatment.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "1."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Supporting calculation of emergency medication doses according to the associated chart and local protocol.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "2."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Selecting appropriately sized airway equipment and other resuscitation supplies when the specific tape provides these recommendations.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "3."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Supporting preparation for pediatric resuscitation, including cardiac arrest and severe respiratory compromise.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "4."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Improving consistency and reducing calculation errors during time-critical care.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "5."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "It is an aid to clinical decision-making, not a substitute for clinical assessment or a current prescribing protocol."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_subsection_4",
          "subsection_title": "3. Parts and functions",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_group_4",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/instrumentation/pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_02.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "A. Measuring scale"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Measures the child’s length according to the tape’s instructions, usually from the crown of the head to the heel with the child lying supine."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/instrumentation/pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_03.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "B. Color-coded zones"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "On color-coded models, the zone identifies an estimated weight category and links to the corresponding chart."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/instrumentation/pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_04.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "C. Dosing chart or reference guide"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Provides model-specific medication and equipment guidance. The exact information varies by product and protocol."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_subsection_5",
          "subsection_title": "4. Advantages",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_group_5",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "list",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "Fast and practical in emergencies.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Reduces reliance on guessing a child’s weight.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Can reduce arithmetic and conversion errors.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "May link medication doses with suitable equipment sizes.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Helps standardize team communication during resuscitation.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Useful when weighing equipment is unavailable or inaccessible.",
                      "level": 0
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_subsection_6",
          "subsection_title": "5. Disadvantages and limitations",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_group_6",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "list",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "Weight is estimated, so the resulting dose may not be exact.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Length does not always reflect actual weight, especially in children with obesity, severe malnutrition or unusual body proportions.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Incorrect positioning or measurement can place a child in the wrong zone.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Charts can be outdated or incompatible with local medication concentrations and protocols.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "A dose calculated from an estimated weight may still be unsafe if the wrong drug concentration, route or unit is selected.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Not every tape contains the same recommendations or uses identical color zones.",
                      "level": 0
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Important: For newborns and young infants, dosing may depend on birth weight, current weight, gestational age and postnatal age. Do not assume a standard length-based emergency tape is appropriate for neonatal drug dosing."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_subsection_7",
          "subsection_title": "6. Preparation and precautions",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_group_7",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "list",
                  "title": "Before using the tape:",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "Confirm that the tape or chart is intended for the child’s age group and the clinical setting.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "1."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Check that it is readable, intact and based on the current approved protocol.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "2."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Ensure the child can be measured safely without delaying urgent resuscitation.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "3."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Identify the appropriate medication reference and verify its version.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "4."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "If a recent, reliable measured weight is available and appropriate for the situation, use it according to the relevant protocol.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "5."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Ensure team members understand the tape’s color zones and the accompanying chart.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "6."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Medication safety checks"
                },
                {
                  "type": "list",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "Confirm the correct drug, indication, dose, route and frequency.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Check whether the prescribed dose is expressed in mg, micrograms, mg/kg or another unit.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Verify the drug concentration and calculate the volume to administer.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Apply the recommended maximum dose and relevant age-specific restrictions.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Use an independent double-check for high-risk medications when required by local policy.",
                      "level": 0
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_subsection_8",
          "subsection_title": "7. How to use it — step-by-step OSCE demonstration",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_group_8",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Step 1: Assess and prepare"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Assess the child’s immediate clinical needs. In an emergency, initiate resuscitation and do not delay lifesaving treatment to obtain a tape measurement."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/instrumentation/pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_05.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Step 2: Position and measure"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "If safe, position the child supine and follow the tape manufacturer’s instructions for measuring length, generally from the crown of the head to the heel. Use the correct anatomical endpoints."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/instrumentation/pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_06.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Step 3: Identify the zone"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Read the child’s length against the tape and identify the corresponding color zone or estimated weight category, if provided."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/instrumentation/pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_07.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Step 4: Consult the matching chart"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Locate the relevant medication or equipment recommendation. Confirm that the chart corresponds to the specific tape and current local protocol."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/instrumentation/pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_08.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Step 5: Verify before administration"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Confirm the drug, dose, concentration, calculated volume, route, maximum dose and patient-specific contraindications. Obtain an independent check when indicated."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Step 6: Administer and reassess"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Administer treatment according to the relevant emergency protocol, document the method used to estimate weight and monitor the child’s response."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_subsection_9",
          "subsection_title": "8. Contraindications and complications",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_group_9",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The tape itself has no major intrinsic contraindication, but its estimates may be unreliable in some circumstances."
                },
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "columns": [
                    "Potential problem",
                    "How to reduce the risk"
                  ],
                  "rows": [
                    [
                      "Incorrect length measurement",
                      "Follow the manufacturer’s measurement instructions carefully."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Weight estimate does not reflect actual body size",
                      "Use clinical judgment and an actual weight when feasible and appropriate."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Wrong chart or color zone",
                      "Match the chart to the exact tape and protocol."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Medication calculation error",
                      "Independently verify the dose, concentration, units and volume."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Delay in emergency treatment",
                      "Begin indicated resuscitation without waiting for measurement."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Inappropriate neonatal dosing",
                      "Use neonatal-specific dosing references based on the relevant clinical variables."
                    ]
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_subsection_10",
          "subsection_title": "9. Normal and abnormal findings",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_group_10",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "This instrument does not produce a physiological finding such as a blood pressure or oxygen saturation. Instead, it provides an estimated weight category."
                },
                {
                  "type": "list",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "Expected result: A clear length reading and an identifiable corresponding zone or weight estimate.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Potentially unreliable result: A measurement that is difficult to obtain, inconsistent with the child’s body habitus, or clearly discordant with a reliable measured weight.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Action when uncertain: Verify the measurement, reassess whether the tape is appropriate, and consult the approved dosing protocol rather than blindly accepting the estimate.",
                      "level": 0
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_subsection_11",
          "subsection_title": "10. Pediatric considerations",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_group_11",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Because the device is designed for pediatric emergencies, its safe use depends on the child’s size, age and clinical circumstances."
                },
                {
                  "type": "list",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "Infants may be difficult to position accurately.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Children with severe malnutrition or obesity may have actual weights that differ substantially from length-based estimates.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Children with abnormal body proportions may not fit the assumptions used by the tape.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Neonates may require dosing based on gestational age, postnatal age and measured weight rather than a standard pediatric tape.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "During cardiac arrest or another time-critical emergency, follow the applicable resuscitation algorithm without allowing tape measurement to delay treatment.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Once a reliable actual weight becomes available, reassess subsequent dosing using the appropriate protocol.",
                      "level": 0
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_subsection_12",
          "subsection_title": "11. Mnemonic — TAPE",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_group_12",
              "group_title": "T",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Take the length"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Measure correctly using the device instructions."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "group_id": "pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_group_13",
              "group_title": "A",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Assign the zone"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Identify the estimated weight category."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "group_id": "pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_group_14",
              "group_title": "P",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Pick the correct protocol"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Use the matching, current medication or equipment chart."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "group_id": "pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_group_15",
              "group_title": "E",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Ensure safety"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Verify dose, concentration, route and maximum dose before administration."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_subsection_13",
          "subsection_title": "12. Common OSCE questions and model answers",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_group_16",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q1. What is this instrument?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "It is a pediatric emergency dosing tape or chart, used to estimate a child’s weight from length and guide emergency medication dosing or equipment selection."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q2. What is the principle behind its use?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "It uses the relationship between a child’s length and expected body weight to provide a rapid estimate, often linked to color-coded recommendations."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q3. Does it measure actual weight?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "No. It estimates weight. An actual measured weight should be used when available and appropriate."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q4. What is the most important precaution before administering a medication?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Verify the drug, dose, concentration, route, calculated volume, maximum dose and applicable patient-specific restrictions against an approved protocol."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q5. Can it be used for every newborn?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "No. Neonatal dosing may require measured weight, gestational age and postnatal age. A standard pediatric length-based tape should not automatically be used for neonatal dosing."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q6. What are its limitations?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "It may be inaccurate in children with obesity, severe malnutrition or unusual body proportions. Incorrect measurement and outdated or mismatched charts can also cause errors."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q7. Should measurement delay treatment in a critically ill child?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "No. Begin indicated emergency care immediately and use the appropriate approved protocol. Do not delay lifesaving interventions to obtain a length measurement."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_subsection_14",
          "subsection_title": "13. Common mistakes and examiner tips",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_group_17",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Common mistakes"
                },
                {
                  "type": "list",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "Calling the tape a weighing scale.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Measuring from the wrong anatomical landmarks.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Reading the wrong color zone.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Using a dosing chart that does not match the tape.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Confusing mg with mL.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Ignoring the drug’s maximum recommended dose.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Assuming an estimated weight is always accurate.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Delaying emergency care while trying to obtain a measurement.",
                      "level": 0
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Examiner tips"
                },
                {
                  "type": "list",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "State that the tape estimates weight rather than measuring it.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Demonstrate the correct positioning and measurement technique.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Explain how you would find the corresponding chart.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Emphasize medication verification and independent double-checks where required.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Mention the limitations in children with abnormal body habitus.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Explain that neonatal dosing may require a different approach.",
                      "level": 0
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_subsection_15",
          "subsection_title": "14. Mini-OSCE practice station",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "pediatric_emergency_dosing_tape_chart_group_18",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Practice station"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Scenario"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "You are given a pediatric emergency dosing tape and its accompanying chart. A child presents to the emergency department with severe respiratory distress. The examiner asks you to demonstrate how you would use the tape safely."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Your tasks"
                },
                {
                  "type": "list",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "Identify the instrument and state its purpose.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "1."
                    },
                    {
